<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What? The 
\f2\i real
\f1\i0  Elvis isn\'92t Estonian.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>By this time Captain Denver was forgetting his stoic role as Sarah\'92s bodyguard/jailer and was foaming for a fight. He almost snapped his pencil.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Steady Cap\'92n Crunch,\'92 Sarah said, warding Captain Denver back to his station with an authoritative wave of her hand.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91According to the prophecy, the statistically normative nationality of Elvis across all universes is North American.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What? That\'92s inconceivable.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It\'92s almost enough to make you give up on prophesying altogether.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It just rips you heart out, that\'92s what it does.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos said, \'91Look. It\'92s not up to us to have an opinion on what nationality\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'97or gender \'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91\'97or ethnicity.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91None of those things matter!\'92 Kleoboulos shouted, becoming short with everyone. \'91What matters is we trust the One After the One, and what he\'97\'92\
